    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "In triangle $ABC$, $BC$ is perpendicular to $AC$.\n\nSide $BC$ has length $a$, side $AC$ has length $b$ and side $AB$ has length $c$.\n\nA quadrant of a circle of radius $x$, centred at $C$, is constructed. The arc meets side $BC$ at $E$. It touches the side $AB$ at $D$, and meets side $AC$ at $F$. The interval $CD$ is perpendicular to $AB$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q14-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 10 p10-q14-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[line width=0.8pt,draw=black,text=black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (C) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (0,3);\n\\coordinate (A) at (6,0);\n\\coordinate (D) at ($(A)!(C)!(B)$);\n\\pgfmathsetmacro{\\quadrantradius}{6/sqrt(5)}\n\\coordinate (E) at (0,\\quadrantradius);\n\\coordinate (F) at (\\quadrantradius,0);\n\\draw (C)--(B)--(A)--cycle;\n\\draw (C)--(D);\n\\draw (F) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=\\quadrantradius];\n\\coordinate (rightA) at ($(D)!0.18cm!(A)$);\n\\coordinate (rightC) at ($(D)!0.18cm!(C)$);\n\\coordinate (rightCorner) at ($(rightA)+(rightC)-(D)$);\n\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (rightA)--(rightCorner)--(rightC);\n\\node[above left] at (B) {$B$};\n\\node[below left] at (C) {$C$};\n\\node[right] at (A) {$A$};\n\\node[above] at (D) {$D$};\n\\node[left] at (E) {$E$};\n\\node[below] at (F) {$F$};\n\\path (B)--(C) node[midway,left] {$a$};\n\\path (C)--(A) node[midway,below=5mm] {$b$};\n\\path (B)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$c$};\n\\path (C)--(D) node[midway,right] {$x$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
