          "description": "Unshaded right triangle with a quadrant centred at C, tangent to AB at D, and perpendicular radius CD. Paired side and radius labels remain attached to their segments.",
          "mathematics": "C=(0,0), B=(0,3), A=(6,0) are illustrative drawing coordinates, not additional givens. D is the perpendicular projection of C onto AB, giving D=(1.2,2.4). The quadrant radius is 6/sqrt(5); E=(0,6/sqrt(5)) and F=(6/sqrt(5),0). Thus D lies on both AB and the quadrant, and CD is perpendicular to AB.",
